        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-30T07:05:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From past experience, if an exception is already pending, then I think this will crash.\n\nLooking at throwException in libcore_io_Linux.cpp, you might want something like:\n\n    jthrowable cause \u003d NULL;\n    if (env-\u003eExceptionCheck()) {\n        cause \u003d env-\u003eExceptionOccurred();\n        env-\u003eExceptionClear();\n    }\n\nMore in general, I think that once an exception is thrown, it\u0027s forbidden to perform pretty much any JNI operation except for releasing resources and returning immediately. See:\n\nhttps://docs.oracle.com/javase/7/docs/technotes/guides/jni/spec/design.html#wp770\n\nwhich lists the only methods that are safe to call with an exception pending.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 36,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 36,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "96c7b4961ddc44d9e487982d72d8dd27c869dffe",
